{"id": "1.2-00015", "case_id": "github_analogdevicesinc_axi_dmac_transfer_direct_v1", "parent_id": null, "source": "github/analogdevicesinc/hdl", "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Agent task and scoring</h2><div class='card'><table><tbody><tr><th style='width:175px'>Input task</th><td class='path'>Project specification, interfaces, and permitted public assets</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Agent context</th><td class='path'>Direct agent workspace: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00015&amp;file_q=public%2F'>public/</a> (13 files)</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Expected output</th><td class='path'>Required RTL: library/axi_dmac/address_generator.v, library/axi_dmac/axi_dmac_burst_memory.v, library/axi_dmac/axi_dmac_ext_sync.v, library/axi_dmac/axi_dmac_framelock.v, library/axi_dmac/axi_dmac_reset_manager.v, library/axi_dmac/axi_dmac_resize_dest.v, library/axi_dmac/axi_dmac_resize_src.v, library/axi_dmac/axi_dmac_response_manager.v and 23 more. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00015&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>Open full output contract</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Hidden reference</th><td class='path'>31 RTL files under private/reference/; <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00015&amp;file=private%2Freference%2Flibrary%2Faxi_dmac%2Faddress_generator.v'>open first reference file</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Private score</th><td class='path'>Passed verification testpoints divided by total testpoints, using testbenches or formal verification<br><strong>2 verification testpoints:</strong> dma_read_shutdown_tb, dma_write_shutdown_tb. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00015&amp;file=private%2Fscoring.json'>Open private scoring contract</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Case-stored agent instruction</h2><div class='card'><p class='muted'>These are case-stored instructions. A launcher may add framing or execution limits; its saved trajectory is the exact runtime record.</p><details><summary>public/instruction.md · <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00015&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>Open raw</a></summary><pre># ADI DMA transfer-engine project\nImplement the complete axi_dmac_transfer engine and every module at the required paths. The original AXI DMAC documentation describes the complete peripheral; this case&#x27;s boundary is its independent transfer engine with request, AXI, AXI-stream, FIFO and diagnostic interfaces. The software AXI-Lite register front-end and board wrappers are outside the case. Consult original documentation, declaration-only interfaces and the reviewed boundary clarifications below. Files provided under support/ are fixed helper includes, not generated module targets.\n\n## Reviewed transfer-engine contract\n- Preserve declared clock domains and active-low reset inputs. ctrl_clk/ctrl_resetn own request control; memory source/destination interfaces use their respective AXI clocks/resets, and ADI FIFO interfaces their declared fifo clocks. Synchronize transfers across domains using the documented ASYNC_CLK parameters. Initial reset is required.\n- DMA_TYPE=0 is AXI memory mapped, 1 AXI stream, 2 ADI FIFO. Source and destination select independently. Bytes flow in increasing-address/little-endian lane order with proper ready/valid and byte-enable behavior. AXI requests obey burst length, size, cache/protection fields, backpressure and completion responses. AXI-stream and ADI FIFO semantics are described in the original manual, including overflow/underflow reporting.\n- A req_valid/req_ready handshake admits a transfer. req_src_address/req_dest_address ports omit their low byte-offset bits; supply word-indexed values according to their declared BYTES_PER_BEAT_WIDTH. req_x_length is bytes minus one; req_y_length is rows minus one when 2D is enabled. Strides advance each row. The request fields remain stable through acceptance. Request completion, measured partial length and end-of-transfer outputs describe drained work, not mere command acceptance.\n- ctrl_enable enables the DMA. Deasserting it must stop new work and eventually drain every AXI request already issued, returning the engine and transaction queues to idle; do not simply gate off an outstanding response. ctrl_pause stalls initiation while preserving active work. Preserve declared request/reset/debug ports; no internal hierarchy names are imposed by this case.\n- Qualification uses both original read- and write-shutdown benches: 32-bit AXI↔ADI-FIFO, FIFO_SIZE=8, DMA_LENGTH_ALIGN=2, aligned address 0x80000000, req_x_length=0x2ff, no 2D/SG/framelock features, independent FIFO clock at twice the AXI clock. After disable, dbg_status must represent drained reset-manager/interface state as exercised by the original bench; responses outstanding in the trusted bus model must be accepted. Preserve parameter interfaces for the rest of the declared closure, but these two benches do not establish exhaustive data, feature or configuration coverage.\n- The exact debug bit definitions are provided in diagnostic_fields.md. This diagnostic contract is externally visible and used by the original shutdown tests. Do not substitute internal implementation names as output requirements.\n- inc_id.vh supplies fixed binary/Gray helper functions and resp.vh supplies AXI response constants. They are retained unchanged and supplied to compilation; implement all31 module files, not these two includes. No arbitrary includes or simulator file/network/process I/O are allowed. Constant elaboration helpers and synthesizable initialization are permitted.\n\nOriginal docs are retained verbatim. These curator clarifications distinguish the transfer engine from its software control front-end and declare the finite evaluated envelope. Score is passed whole testbenches /2; individual transactions are not extra cases or points. The reference RTL and original benches remain private.\n\nSimulation I/O, delays, force/release, final blocks and external includes are forbidden. Constant elaboration functions ($clog2, $unsigned, $signed, $bits) and synthesizable storage initialization are permitted. Save all RTL under the exact required paths; only those files are collected.\n</pre></details></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/4f9003e22a51352ae5c98ae0e20b078c655de5740b778c789229ab1f9d696634.txt", "size": 23650, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case.json"}, {"name": "environment/runtime.json", "url": "assets/9379564162e044e31602be3094e35aa3e6db065b6118a330f0b79ef42b775c9b.txt", "size": 5316, "binary": false, "section": "Other: environment"}, {"name": "private/direct_adapter.json", "url": "assets/41983ec6f64339ef71f8acdad0d3bdf968277a5e38cd9f8f1af38ca1eaf9672d.txt", "size": 683, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/library/axi_dmac/address_generator.v", "url": "assets/097d83addaec1ae8eea9a8e25a83f6b66934ca5a53fe65686e453acb4b3b61bb.txt", "size": 6148, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/library/axi_dmac/axi_dmac_burst_memory.v", "url": "assets/e136955aabd8c0e00b97657f36e53f6a7dd236341084f9ed21e81aec7f2fc99c.txt", "size": 15973, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/library/axi_dmac/axi_dmac_ext_sync.v", "url": "assets/8c4616de243bca6b9dabac6ba098083edc7319d99fc5fb30d712a30caa578427.txt", "size": 3492, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/library/axi_dmac/axi_dmac_framelock.v", "url": "assets/9317827f1b241bbb72218d9cf4c674909a4372959d5de2a7cff456a5b466d7e3.txt", "size": 10983, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/library/axi_dmac/axi_dmac_reset_manager.v", "url": "assets/0531706c60e6754a6460366dc4506b63292fea61dcff5ddbb038ff44938d6916.txt", "size": 10600, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original